--- body ---
## Context

Commit 55a8548 added `.replace("_", "-")` to model slugs in
`src/aedist/plot_census.py` so that pgfplots xticklabels don't hit
unescaped underscores in slide and report builds. The existing
tests in `tests/test_plot_census.py` use sample slugs without
underscores, so the fix is effectively untested — a revert would
regress the slides/report compile silently.

## Scope

Add one test to `tests/test_plot_census.py` that passes a slug
containing `_` to `build_census_rows()` and asserts the output
`model` column contains `-` (no underscores) for that row.

## Test

```python
def test_slug_underscores_replaced_with_dashes():
    metrics = [_synthetic_metric("gpt-5.4_cross", f1=0.8, is_local=False)]
    rows = build_census_rows(metrics)
    assert rows[0]["model"] == "gpt-5.4-cross"
```

## Exit criteria

- New test exists and passes.
- Reverting the `.replace()` line causes the test to fail.
- Trait-verification battery (ADR-5) eventually picks this up when
  green-tests is hooked into the morning healthcheck.
